--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE EFFECTIVE LICENCE OF A BUILD

This module builds three programs: cmd/coax, the scanner and client; cmd/coaxd,
the tuner host; and cmd/fwextract, which extracts firmware from a vendor's own
driver package. They share a module but not a linkage -- coax reaches coaxd over
HTTP and imports none of its packages -- so what a binary carries depends on
which one it is.

Every file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier line, and each falls into one of
three groups.

  Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-or-later
      Written for this module with no third party in it. A recipient takes it
      under either licence, whichever suits.

  GPL-2.0-or-later
      Derived from work under GPL-2.0-or-later. The file's own copyright lines
      say whose, and DERIVED WORK below names the projects.

  GPL-2.0-only
      Derived from work under GPL-2.0-only, likewise named below.

cmd/coax and cmd/fwextract reach nothing outside the first group, so either may
be taken under Apache-2.0 alone. cmd/coaxd reaches all three, so a build of it
is GPL-2.0-only as a whole.

The dual grouping is what lets both hold at once. Apache-2.0 cannot be combined
with GPL-2.0-only, so if the first group were Apache-2.0 alone, coaxd could not
be distributed; the GPL branch is the one coaxd takes.

